          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which drug classes does heart failure guidance describe for reduced ejection fraction?",
          "answer": "Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (40 percent or below) is treated with **four foundational drug classes**, started together or in quick succession. The passage from the heart failure guideline (\"Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction: the four foundational therapy classes,\" from the major cardiology society consensus guidance) cuts off before it names them, so I can't list them from these results.\n\nTwo other points from the retrieved material:\n\n- The heart failure guideline separates heart failure by ejection fraction because the evidence differs between groups. Several of these classes have not shown the same benefit in preserved ejection fraction (50 percent or above).\n- The diabetes guideline (\"Type 2 diabetes: first-line pharmacologic management,\" from the national diabetes association standards of care) names SGLT-2 inhibitors as preferred for heart failure, particularly with reduced ejection fraction. The heart failure guideline describes SGLT-2 inhibitors as the newest addition to this group.\n\nTo get the full list, read the complete heart failure guideline or ask a clinician, who can also explain how these classes apply to a specific situation.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
